I move forward in the market.
There is a fruit cart nearby.
Fresh bananas are kept on the cart.
There is a small cardboard sign there.
The price of bananas is written on the board.
The price is sixty rupees a dozen.
The cart vendor is a young man.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, I want half a dozen bananas."
He selects good bananas.
He puts the bananas in my cloth bag.
I ask him, "Bhaiya, how much is the total?"
He says, "Thirty rupees, Madam."
I do not have exact change.
I give him a large one hundred rupee note.
He takes my note.
He counts the remaining rupees.
He gives me seventy rupees back.
I put the money in my purse.
I say thank you to him.
Then I walk towards the next shop.
